  "goModH1": "h1:xLnfdiJbSp8rNqYEdIW/6eDO4mVoogml14Bh2hSiFpM=",
  "scope": "Complete official module archive, including original LICENSE, module metadata, tests and tooling. No copied cache or git directory. Routing rules gain one optional attribute; no other request or dump field changes.",
  "localChanges": [
    "rule.go Rule: add Protocol uint8 (FRA_PROTOCOL, the rule originator), with the same field name, type, send condition and readback as vishvananda/netlink v1.3.1.",
    "rule_linux.go ruleHandle: send FRA_PROTOCOL when Protocol is nonzero; RuleListFiltered: read FRA_PROTOCOL back into Protocol. Rules without a protocol produce byte-identical requests."
  ],
  "removalCondition": "Remove both root and sing-tun local replace directives and this source copy when an official sagernet/netlink version sends and reads FRA_PROTOCOL through Rule, keeps RuleListFiltered leaving Type and MarkSet unset (bypass and VPNService readback comparisons depend on it), and passes the sing-tun rule ownership tests plus the Linux crash-residue KVM regression.",
